# Commands run by the launchd job com.redwood.demo for the step-13 boot
# (Turnip's Vulkan frame in a real CoreAnimation drawable).
#
# WHAT THIS BOOT IS FOR. turnip_test passed steps 1-12 without ever touching the
# window server: every surface was one the gate made itself and read back in the
# same process. Step 13 is the real link -- a drawable CoreAnimation owns, drawn
# into by Turnip, taken to the panel by the image queue. Two processes ask it,
# because a boot is expensive and they fail separately:
#
#   1  vk_triangle_app --layer   no UIKit: a bare CAMetalLayer of the panel's
#                                size, three frames, the surface imported by its
#                                id, drawn, seed-bumped, presented, read back.
#                                Answers every question except the panel, and its
#                                output is certainly in the log.
#   2  RedwoodVK.app             the application, launched by SpringBoard after
#                                the unlock, drawing a frame every half second.
#                                This is the one a screenshot can prove: green
#                                (or cyan) with a red triangle, colours the Metal
#                                application never draws.
#
# The gate still runs first, so one boot answers both "steps 1-12 still pass"
# and "step 13": a regression in either is visible in the same log.
/redwood/bin/rwtouch wait 60
/redwood/bin/turnip_test
/redwood/bin/vk_triangle_app --layer
/redwood/bin/rwtouch wait 10 notify com.redwood.unlock wait 5
/redwood/bin/battery_test open redwoodvk://
/redwood/bin/rwtouch wait 600
